<h1>TActiveImageButton</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveImageButton" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveImageButton</tt> is the active counterpart of <tt>TImageButton</tt>.
When a <tt>TActiveImageButton</tt> is clicked, rather than a normal post back request a callback request is initiated.
The<tt>OnCallback</tt> event is raised during a callback request and it is raised <b>after</b> the <tt>OnClick</tt> event.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveImageButton</tt> is similar to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.ActiveButton">TActiveButton</a>, except that it displays
the button as an image. <tt>ImageUrl</tt> names the image and <tt>Text</tt> sets its
alternate text. The point where the click landed is carried in the event parameter of the
<tt>OnClick</tt> event, as <tt>X</tt> and <tt>Y</tt>, and not in the parameter of
<tt>OnCallback</tt>. A handler that needs the coordinate therefore uses <tt>OnClick</tt>.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Attribute rewritten</th></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageUrl</tt></td><td><tt>src</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>AlternateText</tt></td><td><tt>alt</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageAlign</tt></td><td><tt>align</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>DescriptionUrl</tt></td><td><tt>longdesc</tt></td></tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
Each update is subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>. <tt>ImageAlign</tt> and
<tt>DescriptionUrl</tt> are deprecated, as they are on
<a href="?page=Controls.Image">TImage</a>.
</p>
